   "id": "chem.water-ionization",
   "name": "The ion product of water, Kw",
   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Water ionizes very slightly: 2H₂O ⇌ H₃O⁺ + OH⁻. At 25 °C, Kw = [H₃O⁺][OH⁻] = 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁴ in every aqueous solution, so in pure water both ions are 1.0 × 10⁻⁷ M. A solution is neutral when [H₃O⁺] = [OH⁻], acidic when [H₃O⁺] is larger and basic when [OH⁻] is larger. Kw changes with temperature."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "ውሃ በጣም ትንሽ ይዮናይዛል። በ25 °C Kw = [H₃O⁺][OH⁻] = 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁴። ንፁህ ውሃ ውስጥ ሁለቱም 1.0 × 10⁻⁷ M ናቸው።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
